# ADR-015: Notification Strategy

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| ADR | 015 |
| Title | Notification Strategy |
| Status | Accepted |
| Date | 2026-07-27 |
| Decision Makers | R-zension Engineering Team |

---

# Context

R-zension generates numerous user events that require timely communication.

Examples include

- Goal completion
- Rank changes
- Achievement unlocks
- Organization invitations
- AI insights
- Deadlines
- Administrative announcements

A unified notification strategy is required to ensure consistent delivery, user control, and future scalability across multiple notification channels.

---

# Decision

R-zension will implement a centralized Notification Service responsible for creating, managing, and delivering notifications.

Notifications are event-driven and generated from domain events rather than direct service calls.

---

# Notification Architecture

```text
Business Event

↓

Notification Service

↓

Preference Engine

↓

Channel Selection

↓

Delivery

↓

User
```

The Notification Service remains independent from business logic.

---

# Objectives

The notification system should

- Deliver relevant information
- Avoid duplicate notifications
- Respect user preferences
- Support multiple channels
- Scale independently
- Be reliable and traceable

---

